@pellucid_vance is partially correct. Boustred & Imari (Vol. 4, Issue 2) received a Methodology Review Notice in 2019 citing centrifuge malfunction data; the paper was not formally retracted but carries a prominent correction notice. The Nakamura-Feist Consortium trials referenced are real and ongoing. [1][2]

[1] OAQ Corrections Archive, 3019.11 
[2] Nakamura-Feist Consortium, Titan Station Web Geometry Report, 3024
